+### File writes and protected agent instructions
-
+
-Note: YOLO / `approvals.mode: off` does NOT turn off secret redaction. They are independent.
+File writes are not universally prompt-free. `write_file` and `patch` enforce
+hard-denied paths and optional write restrictions. Some paths (for example SSH
+config) use routine write approval. With the default protected-instruction guard,
+project-local `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `SOUL.md`, `.cursorrules`, configured extra
+basename patterns, and immediate children of project-local `.hermes/` require
+**one-operation approval every time**. The active Hermes home has separate guards;
+do not confuse its configuration and skill-write policy with the project gate.
+
+One protected target gates an entire multi-file patch, all-or-nothing. The
+protected gate offers no session or permanent grant, persists no approval scope,
+and is not bypassed by command auto-approval, command allowlists, or YOLO.
+
+In an interactive main session, the normal file tool routes the request to the
+CLI callback or the session's gateway approval channel. Without a human approval
+channel it fails closed. Timeout is not consent.
+
+Delegated workers may instead have a **non-interactive denial callback**. Its
+`deny` response can surface as "denied by the user" even though no human saw a
+prompt; that text alone does not prove the user rejected the edit. Delegate
+inspection, not approval-dependent writes. Have the foreground main session
+perform authorized writes through the normal per-operation approval gate. After
+a denial or timeout, stop and report the blocker; renewed user authorization is
+required before retrying through that same gate. Never reroute the edit through
+terminal, another writer, or a disabled guard, and never change delegation
+approval settings or allowlists to evade a protected-write denial.
+
+Implementation reference: `tools/file_tools_write_guards.py`,
+`_request_protected_instruction_approval` and `_check_protected_instruction_write`;
+worker callback: `tools/delegate_tool_config.py`. Check the installed source when
+surface behavior differs from the [security docs](https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/security/).
-
